    "body": "I ran a web compat check for #9426 with a Firefox build that can switch between Gecko's current behavior, Chromium's, and #9426. I think #9426 is web compatible. The only visible changes were in sandboxed iframes without `allow-scripts`, where noscript content stops rendering. That broke 2 pages out of the ~1,000 checked.\n\nAI summary of the research ([zcorpan/noscript-compat-10879](https://github.com/zcorpan/noscript-compat-10879)):\n\n> **Method.** One Firefox build with a pref for the three behaviors (the Chromium-like mode matched Chrome Canary on all 16 probes). The pages come from Chromium's use counters 5857–5861, which 59,711 pages hit in the 2026-10-01 desktop crawl. I used a random sample of 100 per counter, plus the top 100 per counter. Each page was loaded live in all three modes and compared visually. Every page that hit was also traced at runtime to see what scripts do with the parsed noscript content. Every call site that used it had its code reviewed.\n>\n> **Results**, extrapolated to the 59,711 pages:\n>\n> | #9426 vs | Visible change | Non-visual, user-facing | Tracking fetches only |\n> |---|---|---|---|\n> | Gecko today | ~2 worse, ~2 neutral (sandboxed iframes) | 0 found (≤2,163) | ~1,300 |\n> | Chromium | same | 1 found, an improvement | ~5,700 |\n>\n> **Affected pages:**\n>\n> - Worse: mancity.bg ([crop](https://github.com/zcorpan/noscript-compat-10879/blob/main/2026-10-01/random/out/review/069-CvsA2.png)) and dominikaner-braunschweig.de ([crop](https://github.com/zcorpan/noscript-compat-10879/blob/main/out/review/468-CvsA2.png)). Noscript `<img>` fallbacks in sandboxed iframes disappear.\n> - Improvement vs Chromium: on equity.wwu.edu, a hidden noscript `<input id=search-box>` no longer takes the visible search field's label.\n> - Neutral: on everythingfor420.com, after a cart drawer refresh, Enter in a quantity field goes to checkout instead of the cart page, as on a fresh load.\n>\n> Gecko today and Chromium showed no visible difference from each other. Nothing like the oreo-promo.com hydration mismatch (https://bugzil.la/1931348) showed up.\n>\n> Details are in the [README](https://github.com/zcorpan/noscript-compat-10879/blob/main/README.md).\n",
